From: OpenWrt vendor-wifi bring-up
Subject: [PATCH] net: wireless: make the WEXT Kconfig symbols selectable

The vendor mt_wifi driver registers net_device.wireless_handlers and serves
its private ioctls (iwpriv) through WEXT.  LEDE's 6.12+ generic config sets
the WEXT symbols to "not set", but WIRELESS_EXT/WEXT_PRIV are invisible
Kconfig symbols, so a value written into target/linux/generic/config-6.x is
dropped again by olddefconfig.  Give the two symbols a prompt so the config
fragment sticks.  WEXT_SPY no longer exists in 6.18.

Signed-off-by: Jiyun A10 vendor-wifi bring-up
---
--- a/net/wireless/Kconfig
+++ b/net/wireless/Kconfig
@@ -1,6 +1,6 @@
 # SPDX-License-Identifier: GPL-2.0-only
 config WIRELESS_EXT
-	bool
+	bool "Wireless extensions"
 
 config WEXT_CORE
 	def_bool y
@@ -12,7 +12,7 @@
 	depends on WEXT_CORE
 
 config WEXT_PRIV
-	bool
+	bool "WEXT_PRIV"
 
 config CFG80211
 	tristate "cfg80211 - wireless configuration API"
